        "answerHtml": "<!-- QUESTION 1: JULY 2022 (MAIN) Q.5c [5 MARKS] -->\n        <div class=\"q-block\">\n          <div class=\"q-header\">\n            <span class=\"q-badge\">MPMSU July 2022 (Main) — Q.5c [5 Marks]</span>\n            <span class=\"q-weight\">Short Note | Target: 2–3 Handwritten Pages</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"q-text-prompt\">\n            <strong>Exam Question:</strong> Short Note: Tabulation - Principles, parts of a table and rules for constructing statistical tables (5 Marks).\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"q-answer-content\">\n            <div class=\"ans-part\">\n              <div class=\"ans-part-title\">Comprehensive Clinical Answer: Statistical Tabulation</div>\n              <div class=\"ans-part-body\">\n                <p><strong>Definition:</strong> Tabulation is the systematic, logical presentation of numerical quantitative and qualitative data in rows (horizontal) and columns (vertical), designed to simplify complex data, facilitate comparison, save space, and provide a basis for statistical analysis.</p>\n\n                <p><strong>1. Essential Component Parts of a Statistical Table:</strong></p>\n                <ol>\n                  <li><strong>Table Number:</strong> Clear identifying number placed at the top (e.g., Table 4.1).</li>\n                  <li><strong>Title:</strong> Concise, self-explanatory statement answering: <em>What, Where, When, and How</em> data are classified.</li>\n                  <li><strong>Stub:</strong> The extreme left-hand column containing row headings / classifications.</li>\n                  <li><strong>Caption (Box Head):</strong> The column headings and sub-headings at the top of the columns.</li>\n                  <li><strong>Body:</strong> The core interior containing the actual numerical figures in cells formed by row-column intersections.</li>\n                  <li><strong>Prefatory Note / Headnote:</strong> Brief explanatory note below title specifying measurement units (e.g., \"Values in thousands\").</li>\n                  <li><strong>Footnote:</strong> Placed at the bottom to clarify abbreviations, specific cells, or statistical symbols (* $p < 0.05$).</li>\n                  <li><strong>Source Note:</strong> Cites the original source of secondary data.</li>\n                </ol>\n\n                <p><strong>2. Core Principles & Rules of Tabulation:</strong></p>\n                <ul>\n                  <li>Tables should be self-explanatory without requiring reader to search the text.</li>\n                  <li>Units of measurement must be clearly stated in the column/row headings.</li>\n                  <li>Rows and columns should include sub-totals and grand totals for verification.</li>\n                  <li>If data are missing or zero, use \"0\" or \"—\" rather than leaving cells blank.</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- ============================================================== -->\n  <!-- 4. CHILD HEALTH NURSING (CHN / PEDIATRICS)                     -->\n  <!-- ============================================================== -->"
